      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita</code></strong> Two figures go into the <em>Waveforms</em> section, and the decibel formula goes into the <em>Amplitude</em> definition.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\n+++ b/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\n@@ -13,6 +13,24 @@\n       \u003cp>Sound travels through air as a continuous \u003cterm>waveform\u003c/term> of pressure changes.\n       A microphone converts these pressure changes into an electrical signal.\n       To store the signal digitally, the computer takes thousands of measurements, called \u003cterm>samples\u003c/term>, of the signal's amplitude every second.\u003c/p>\n+      \u003cfig id=\"fig-waveform\">\n+        \u003ctitle>A recorded waveform, with clipping at the right\u003c/title>\n+        \u003cimage href=\"../images/waveform.png\" placement=\"break\" scale=\"80\">\n+          \u003calt>A waveform whose peaks are cut flat at the right-hand end\u003c/alt>\n+        \u003c/image>\n+      \u003c/fig>\n+      \u003cp>Drawn schematically, one cycle of a pure tone looks like this:\u003c/p>\n+      \u003cfig>\n+        \u003ctitle>One cycle of a sine wave\u003c/title>\n+        \u003csvg-container>\n+          \u003csvg:svg xmlns:svg=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"320\" height=\"120\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 120\">\n+            \u003csvg:line x1=\"0\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#999\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n+            \u003csvg:path d=\"M0,60 C40,0 80,0 120,60 S200,120 240,60 S300,20 320,45\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3c78c8\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n+            \u003csvg:text x=\"8\" y=\"16\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#333\">amplitude\u003c/svg:text>\n+            \u003csvg:text x=\"270\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#333\">time\u003c/svg:text>\n+          \u003c/svg:svg>\n+        \u003c/svg-container>\n+      \u003c/fig>\n     \u003c/section>\n     \u003csection>\n       \u003ctitle>Sample rate\u003c/title>\n@@ -57,7 +75,22 @@\n         \u003cdlentry>\n           \u003cdt>Amplitude\u003c/dt>\n           \u003cdd>The height of a sound wave, corresponding to how loud the sound is.\n-          Measured in decibels (dB).\u003c/dd>\n+          Measured in decibels (dB), a ratio against a reference level:\n+          \u003cequation-block>\n+            \u003cmathml>\n+              \u003cm:math xmlns:m=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\n+                \u003cm:mrow>\n+                  \u003cm:msub>\u003cm:mi>L\u003c/m:mi>\u003cm:mtext>dB\u003c/m:mtext>\u003c/m:msub>\n+                  \u003cm:mo>=\u003c/m:mo>\n+                  \u003cm:mn>20\u003c/m:mn>\n+                  \u003cm:msub>\u003cm:mi>log\u003c/m:mi>\u003cm:mn>10\u003c/m:mn>\u003c/m:msub>\n+                  \u003cm:mfrac>\u003cm:mi>A\u003c/m:mi>\u003cm:msub>\u003cm:mi>A\u003c/m:mi>\u003cm:mn>0\u003c/m:mn>\u003c/m:msub>\u003c/m:mfrac>\n+                \u003c/m:mrow>\n+              \u003c/m:math>\n+            \u003c/mathml>\n+            \u003cph>L (dB) = 20 log10 (A / A0)\u003c/ph>\n+          \u003c/equation-block>\n+          A level of \u003cequation-inline>\u003cmathml>\u003cm:math xmlns:m=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\u003cm:mrow>\u003cm:mo>−\u003c/m:mo>\u003cm:mn>6\u003c/m:mn>\u003cm:mtext>dB\u003c/m:mtext>\u003c/m:mrow>\u003c/m:math>\u003c/mathml>\u003cph>−6 dB\u003c/ph>\u003c/equation-inline> is half the amplitude of the reference.\u003c/dd>\n         \u003c/dlentry>\n         \u003cdlentry>\n           \u003cdt>Clipping\u003c/dt>"} lang="diff" title="topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the figure elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;fig&gt;</code> is a figure: a <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> and some content, numbered in output. Give it an <code>@id</code> when something links to it, as <code>fig-waveform</code> is linked from the recording task.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;image href="…"&gt;</code> places an image. <code>@placement="break"</code> puts it on its own line rather than inline with the text; <code>@scale="80"</code> renders it at 80 percent of its size. <code>@href</code> is relative to the topic file, hence <code>../images/</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;alt&gt;</code> is the text alternative, read by screen readers and shown when the image cannot be. Describe the information that the image conveys.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;svg-container&gt;</code> holds inline SVG. The SVG elements must carry the <code>svg:</code> prefix, <code>&lt;svg:svg xmlns:svg="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;</code>, because that is how the DITA DTDs declare them; an unprefixed <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code> does not validate.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the equation elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;equation-block&gt;</code> is a displayed equation; <code>&lt;equation-inline&gt;</code> is one inside a sentence. Both are from the equation domain, which the base DTDs include.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;mathml&gt;</code> holds MathML, here with the <code>m:</code> prefix bound to the MathML namespace. The formula is <code>L(dB) = 20 log10 (A / A0)</code>.</li>
      <li>The <code>&lt;ph&gt;</code> beside each <code>&lt;mathml&gt;</code> is a text alternative. The spec allows an equation to carry several representations; a processor uses the one it can render.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>DITA-OT 4.3.5's HTML5 transform drops <code>&lt;mathml&gt;</code>, which is a <code>foreign</code> specialization, unless a MathML plugin is installed. That is why each equation keeps a <code>&lt;ph&gt;</code> text alternative beside the MathML: the HTML shows the text form, and a processor that renders MathML shows the formula. You can inspect this by rebuilding the guide after adding the figures.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <h2 id="step-3-an-image-map" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 3: An image map<a href="#step-3-an-image-map" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/recording-your-first-track.dita</code></strong> The Device Toolbar step gets an <code>&lt;imagemap&gt;</code>, and the waveform step gets a cross-reference to the figure by its id.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\n+++ b/topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\n@@ -22,13 +22,29 @@\n         \u003ccmd>Select your microphone from the recording device list in the \u003cuicontrol>Device Toolbar\u003c/uicontrol>.\u003c/cmd>\n         \u003cinfo>\n           \u003cp>The \u003cuicontrol>Device Toolbar\u003c/uicontrol> is near the top of the window.\n-          The recording device list has a microphone icon next to it.\u003c/p>\n+          The recording device list has a microphone icon next to it.\n+          Click a control in the picture to read about it.\u003c/p>\n+          \u003cimagemap>\n+            \u003cimage href=\"../images/device-toolbar.png\">\n+              \u003calt>The Device Toolbar: audio host, recording device, channels and playback device\u003c/alt>\n+            \u003c/image>\n+            \u003carea>\n+              \u003cshape>rect\u003c/shape>\n+              \u003ccoords>170,20,370,60\u003c/coords>\n+              \u003cxref href=\"preparing-to-record.dita\">Recording device\u003c/xref>\n+            \u003c/area>\n+            \u003carea>\n+              \u003cshape>rect\u003c/shape>\n+              \u003ccoords>380,20,490,60\u003c/coords>\n+              \u003cxref href=\"what-is-digital-audio.dita\">Channels\u003c/xref>\n+            \u003c/area>\n+          \u003c/imagemap>\n         \u003c/info>\n       \u003c/step>\n       \u003cstep>\n         \u003ccmd>Click \u003cuicontrol>Record\u003c/uicontrol>, or press \u003cuicontrol>R\u003c/uicontrol>, to start recording.\u003c/cmd>\n         \u003cinfo>\n-          \u003cp>A blue waveform appears as Audacity captures audio from your microphone.\u003c/p>\n+          \u003cp>A blue waveform appears as Audacity captures audio from your microphone, like \u003cxref href=\"what-is-digital-audio.dita#what-is-digital-audio/fig-waveform\"/>.\u003c/p>\n           \u003cnote type=\"warning\">A flat line instead of a waveform means the microphone is not selected correctly.\n           Click \u003cuicontrol>Stop\u003c/uicontrol> and check the recording device.\u003c/note>\n         \u003c/info>"} lang="diff" title="topics/recording-your-first-track.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the image map elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;imagemap&gt;</code> is an <code>&lt;image&gt;</code> followed by one or more <code>&lt;area&gt;</code> elements. It is from the utilities domain.</li>
      <li>Each <code>&lt;area&gt;</code> has a <code>&lt;shape&gt;</code> (<code>rect</code>, <code>circle</code> or <code>poly</code>), <code>&lt;coords&gt;</code> in pixels of the image, and an <code>&lt;xref&gt;</code> for the link. Here the <code>&lt;xref&gt;</code> elements have content, so the link text is the given label rather than the target's title.</li>
      <li>The cross-reference <code>what-is-digital-audio.dita#what-is-digital-audio/fig-waveform</code> reaches the figure by its <code>@id</code>, the same <code>file#topic/element</code> form as a section link in stage 07.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-4-update-the-readme-and-run-the-gate" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 4: Update the README and run the gate<a href="#step-4-update-the-readme-and-run-the-gate" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Change the "You are on" line and the layout</strong> The layout section gains the <code>images/</code> folder.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n Build a guide through 27 stages. Maps begin at stage 02; HTML publication begins at stage 03.\n \n-You are on stage 07: links.\n+You are on stage 08: figures.\n \n ## Stages\n "} lang="diff" title="README.md" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Format and check</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml format -i topics/*.dita\nscripts/check-stage.sh"} lang="bash" />
      <CodeBlock code={"== validate-project  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\n9 file(s): 9 valid, 0 invalid.\n\n== project-health  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\nRoot map: none (none configured); house rules: none (none configured)\nProject is healthy: valid, no broken references, keys, orphans, or broken element ids.\n\n== build  skipped (no project.json yet) ==\n\nSTAGE OK"} lang="plaintext" />
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p><code>project-health</code> checks image references too. Misspell <code>waveform.png</code> in the <code>&lt;fig&gt;</code> and run the gate to see the broken reference.</p>
      <p>After each error exercise, undo the deliberate change and rerun the gate. Confirm that it prints <code>STAGE OK</code> before continuing.</p>
      <h2 id="publish-your-changes" class="group scroll-mt-20">Publish your changes<a href="#publish-your-changes" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>Add the lesson's topics to <code>audacity-guide.ditamap</code>, then rebuild the guide. The complete map at this checkpoint is:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE map PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Map//EN\" \"map.dtd\">\n\n\u003cmap>\n  \u003ctitle>Audio user guide\u003c/title>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/exporting-audio.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/installing-audacity.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/preparing-to-record.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/removing-background-noise.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/trimming-audio.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\"/>\n\u003c/map>"} lang="xml" title="audacity-guide.ditamap" />
      <CodeBlock code={"dita --project=project.json --output=out\npython3 scripts/check-output-links.py out"} lang="bash" />
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;fig&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> and an <code>@id</code>; <code>&lt;image&gt;</code> with <code>@href</code>, <code>@placement</code>, <code>@scale</code> and an <code>&lt;alt&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li>Image paths are relative to the topic, so a sibling <code>images/</code> folder is <code>../images/</code>.</li>
      <li>Inline SVG goes in <code>&lt;svg-container&gt;</code> with the <code>svg:</code> prefix.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;equation-block&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;equation-inline&gt;</code> carry <code>&lt;mathml&gt;</code> plus a <code>&lt;ph&gt;</code> text alternative; HTML5 output needs the alternative.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;imagemap&gt;</code>: an image, then <code>&lt;area&gt;</code> elements with <code>&lt;shape&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;coords&gt;</code> and an <code>&lt;xref&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li>End of Part 1: nine topics, every base element you need for the body of a guide, published through the map and build introduced in stages 02 and 03.</li>
      </ul>
